Subject: SLA/Hollowing.cpp: keep the drain-hole geometry, leave the OpenVDB part out

Layer::make_contour_z (ContourZ.cpp, the z-contouring of the top surface) uses sla::IndexedMesh, and IndexedMesh::query_ray_hit asks
sla::DrainHole::get_intersections, which is plain geometry in SLA/Hollowing.cpp. The rest of that file (the hollowing of a mesh and the cutting
of drain holes out of slices) needs OpenVDB, which orca_core does not build. With ORCA_CORE_SLICING_ONLY defined the file keeps DrainHole and
leaves the rest out; without the symbol it is as Orca has it.
Orca Slicer v2.5.2, commit f92a7c065c5718b8ef1baac1cd704df2911238f4.

diff --git a/src/libslic3r/SLA/Hollowing.cpp b/src/libslic3r/SLA/Hollowing.cpp
index db8402e6..3e966051 100644
